<header class="hero hero-sm">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>MONDAY</h1>
    <div class="line">
      <span class="chip">Monday 14 September</span>
      <p>Baselines start today. None of them are tests you can fail.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="wrap">

  <div class="tl" id="tl">
    <div class="tl-row" data-from="09:30" data-to="10:00">
      <div class="tl-time">9:30 - 10:00<small>30 minutes</small></div>
      <div class="tl-card tl-breathe">
        <h3>Breathe in</h3>
        <p>Coming in and settling. Nobody will ask you anything yet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tl-row" data-from="10:00" data-to="10:30">
      <div class="tl-time">10:00 - 10:30<small>30 minutes</small></div>
      <a class="tl-card tl-make" href="#phse">
        <h3>PHSE</h3>
        <p>Every morning now, first thing.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="tl-row" data-from="10:30" data-to="11:15">
      <div class="tl-time">10:30 - 11:15<small>45 minutes</small></div>
      <a class="tl-card tl-work" href="#english">
        <h3>English</h3>
        <p>Baseline first, then your own shelf.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="tl-row" data-from="11:15" data-to="12:00">
      <div class="tl-time">11:15 - 12:00<small>45 minutes</small></div>
      <a class="tl-card tl-make" href="#forest">
        <h3>Forest School</h3>
        <p>Outside, whatever the weather is doing.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="tl-row" data-from="12:00" data-to="12:30">
      <div class="tl-time">12:00 - 12:30<small>30 minutes</small></div>
      <div class="tl-card tl-break">
        <h3>Lunch</h3>
        <p></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tl-row" data-from="12:30" data-to="13:30">
      <div class="tl-time">12:30 - 1:30<small>60 minutes</small></div>
      <a class="tl-card tl-work" href="#maths">
        <h3>Maths</h3>
        <p>Baseline first, then your own shelf.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="tl-row" data-from="13:30" data-to="14:00">
      <div class="tl-time">1:30 - 2:00<small>30 minutes</small></div>
      <a class="tl-card tl-key" href="#project">
        <h3>Project</h3>
        <p>Half an hour on your own thing.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="tl-row" data-from="14:00" data-to="14:30">
      <div class="tl-time">2:00 - 2:30<small>30 minutes</small></div>
      <div class="tl-card tl-breathe">
        <h3>Breathe out</h3>
        <p>Winding down. Say what was alright about today, or say nothing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="stripnote">The times are when things are happening, not orders. If a session is not working for you today, saying so is a reasonable thing to do.</p>

  <details class="acc acc-orange anchor" id="baseline">
    <summary>
      <div class="txt">
        <h2>About this week</h2>
        <p>Why there is a baseline in nearly every session.</p>
      </div>
      <svg class="chev" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0a2f38" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="body">
      <p>A baseline is a starting mark. Jay needs to know what you can already do so that what he sets you next is the right level. That is the whole reason for it.</p>
      <div class="grid3">
        <div class="mini"><span class="n">Not a test</span>No grade, no mark out of ten, nothing on a report.</div>
        <div class="mini"><span class="n">Skip freely</span>Anything you do not fancy answering, leave blank and move on.</div>
        <div class="mini"><span class="n">Once</span>These happen this week and then they are done.</div>
      </div>
      <p>If one turns into too much, stopping halfway is fine. Where you stopped tells Jay something useful as well.</p>

    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="acc acc-plum anchor" id="phse">
    <summary>
      <div class="txt">
        <h2>PHSE</h2>
        <p>Half an hour, every morning, before anything else.</p>
      </div>
      <svg class="chev" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#f7f2e9" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="body">
      <p>PHSE is on every morning now, in the same slot, before anything else. It is talking rather than writing, and there is nothing to hand in at the end of it.</p>
      <div class="grid3">
        <div class="mini"><span class="n">Join in</span>Say what you think when you have something to say.</div>
        <div class="mini"><span class="n">Listen</span>Take it in and say nothing. That still counts.</div>
        <div class="mini"><span class="n">Step out</span>Leave the room and come back when you want to.</div>
      </div>
      <p>Willow leads it. She is new here this term, so she is finding her feet in Base 5 the same as everyone else.</p>
      <p class="chiplabel">Other ways to do it</p>
      <div class="chips">
        <span class="way">Write it down instead of saying it</span>
        <span class="way">Answer only the bits you want to</span>
        <span class="way">Sit at the edge of the room</span>
        <span class="way">Skip it</span>
      </div>

    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="acc acc-bright anchor" id="english">
    <summary>
      <div class="txt">
        <h2>English</h2>
        <p>Baseline first, then your own shelf.</p>
      </div>
      <svg class="chev" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#f7f2e9" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="body">
      <p>The baseline comes first and it is short. After that it is your own shelf, same as last week.</p>
      <div class="chips" style="margin-bottom:6px">
        <a class="btn btn-orange" href="/practice/#english-gcse">GCSE english</a>
        <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/practice/#english-standard">Standard english</a>
      </div>
      <p>Anything you write can be sent to Jay from the activity itself.</p>

    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="acc acc-teal anchor" id="forest">
    <summary>
      <div class="txt">
        <h2>Forest School</h2>
        <p>Outside for three quarters of an hour.</p>
      </div>
      <svg class="chev" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#f7f2e9" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="body">
      <p>Outside whatever the weather is doing, so coats on if it is that sort of morning.</p>
      <p>Jay is building something for this session later in the term. For now it happens in the room rather than on a screen. If you want something on a screen afterwards, the <a href="/practice/">practice shelves</a> are open.</p>

    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="acc acc-yellow anchor" id="maths">
    <summary>
      <div class="txt">
        <h2>Maths</h2>
        <p>Baseline first, then your own shelf.</p>
      </div>
      <svg class="chev" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0a2f38" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="body">
      <p>The baseline shows Jay where to start you. After that, pick the shelf that matches what he has set you.</p>
      <div class="chips" style="margin-bottom:6px">
        <a class="btn btn-orange" href="/practice/#maths-gcse">GCSE maths</a>
        <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/practice/#maths-standard">Standard maths</a>
      </div>
      <p>Your fifteen targets for this half term are on <a href="/my-targets.html">My targets</a>, behind your PIN.</p>

    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="acc acc-orange anchor" id="project">
    <summary>
      <div class="txt">
        <h2>Project</h2>
        <p>Thirty minutes on your own thing.</p>
      </div>
      <svg class="chev" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0a2f38" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="body">
      <p>Short slot, so it is picking something small rather than starting something big. Your page is behind your code.</p>
      <div class="chips" style="margin-bottom:6px">
        <a class="btn btn-orange" href="/projects/">My project</a>
      </div>
      <p>The autumn question is still what if dinosaurs still existed. If you have not picked a direction yet, that is what this half hour is for.</p>

    </div>
  </details>

  <div class="sendbox" style="border-style:solid">
    <p class="sendtitle">Want Jay to see something you did today?</p>
    <p class="sendwhy">Anything at all. The writing pad and the practice activities both have a send button at the bottom of them.</p>
    <div class="sendrow">
      <a class="btn btn-orange" href="/tools/write.html">Open the writing pad</a>
      <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/practice/">Practice</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <a class="backlink" href="/">Back to the week</a>

</div>

